Qwen3.8-Flash-Next abliterated - fngine

Installer recipe
----------------
Adapted from the fafstmobel - Cinference installer:
https://github.com/satellitedown/fafstmobel-cinference
The recipe has been changed to build fngine instead of Cinference, pin CUDA 13.3
with a separately probed CUDA host compiler, check the CPU's AVX-512 extensions,
download the abliterated Qwen3.8-Flash-Next fngine pack with per-file checksums,
and keep the server's learned placement statistics across updates.

This repository provides an Apache-2.0 installation recipe. It does not
redistribute model weights. Its license does not replace the licenses of
downloaded software or model artifacts.

Runtime
-------
fngine: https://github.com/satellitedown/fngine (Apache-2.0)
The immutable runtime revision is recorded in runtime-manifest.json. fngine is
derived in part from Cinference (https://github.com/satellitedown/cinference)
and NInfer (https://github.com/Neroued/ninfer, Apache-2.0), with GGUF i-quant
code from ggml (MIT) and vendored libraries under their own licenses; see
fngine's NOTICE and LICENSE. This recipe builds the pinned commit without local
source patches.

Model
-----
satellitedown/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-abliterated-fngine:
https://huggingface.co/satellitedown/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-abliterated-fngine
The immutable model revision and the SHA-256 of every downloaded file are
recorded in runtime-manifest.json. The download retains the model repository's
LICENSE, NOTICE and README.md without alteration.

Upstream inputs (see the downloaded NOTICE):
- Qwen: Qwen/Qwen3.8-Flash-Next, Qwen Community License 1.0. The pack is a
  derivative work and the license's conditions apply to it.
- ISTA-DASLab: Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-GSQ-RCO-GGUF (IQ3_S); GSQ and RCO
  quantization of the routed experts and n-gram table, kept byte-identical.
- huihui-ai: Huihui-Qwen3.8-Flash-Next-abliterated; its edited dense tensors
  are included and its routed-expert edit is applied by fngine at run time.
  No retraining was performed.
- NVIDIA: CUDA components downloaded from PyPI retain their own license terms.

